## Quick Mental Model

```text
Object is no longer needed
          ↓
Is it still reachable?
      ↙          ↘
    No            Yes
     ↓             ↓
GC can remove   Possible leak
     ↓             ↓
Memory freed   Memory stays used
```

### In One Sentence

> **A Java memory leak occurs when objects that are no longer needed are still reachable, preventing the garbage collector from reclaiming their memory.**

